IO-26: convert wind speed from a user-prepared climate file to mph

ClimateFileReader::parseUserLine() stored the wind speed column as read, and
SWMMEngine::stepRunoff() uses it as mph. The manual says a user-prepared
climate file gives wind speed in km/hour for metric units, as the WINDSPEED
MONTHLY values are. In SI models the file's wind speed was used 1.608 times
too large in rain-on-snow melt and reported 1.608 times too large by
swmm_climate_get_wind_speed(). Divide by 1.608 (the WINDSPEED conversion
factor) for SI units when the value is read, as the legacy patch does. US
models are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-26_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydrology/ClimateFile.cpp b/src/engine/hydrology/ClimateFile.cpp
index cd3de11..0caa388 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydrology/ClimateFile.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydrology/ClimateFile.cpp
@@ -297,9 +297,11 @@ void ClimateFileReader::parseUserLine(const char* line) {
     if (s2[0] != '\0' && s2[0] != '*') {
         file_data_[EVAP][d] = std::atof(s2);
     }
-    // WIND
+    // WIND (user units: km/hr for SI → mph, legacy UCF(WINDSPEED) = 1.608)
     if (s3[0] != '\0' && s3[0] != '*') {
-        file_data_[WIND][d] = std::atof(s3);
+        double v = std::atof(s3);
+        if (unit_system_ == 1) v /= 1.608;
+        file_data_[WIND][d] = v;
     }
 }
 
